I look around the supermarket.
I cannot find the milk.
I see a young employee in the shop.
"Excuse me, where is the milk?" I ask.
He smiles and points.
"It is over there, by the butter," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I walk over there.
There are many fridges.
It is cold here.
But here is the milk!
I take a carton of milk.
Beside the milk lies the cheese.
I look at the cheese.
I also take a block of cheese.
Now I have almost everything on my list.
